{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/688727-the-martial-arts-thread","id":688727,"title":"The Martial Arts Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-04T14:05:19-07:00","id":688727,"title":"The Martial Arts Thread","content":"Gamers and geeks can often carry the image of the classic &quot;wimpy kid&quot;. Sometimes, that's totally accurate. Sometimes, it's completely wrong. People are diverse in their backgrounds and interests, and sometimes they learn to fight for one reason or another.<br /> <br /> As for the geek angle on this, it's generations deep. The first tabletop rpg games were based on miniature war simulation games on graph paper, which says something in itself, but even Dungeons and Dragons had warriors, knights, etc. Trained combatants. Fighting with a melee weapon is just as much a part of the martial arts as unarmed combat, but as role playing games evolved we got brawler archetypes; everything from Final Fantasy monks and black belts, World of Warcraft Kung Fu Pandareans to White Wolf's own short-lived version of Street Fighter (if someone has a copy, let me know. I would gladly take it off your hands, and at a handsome price if needed. PLEASE BRING THIS PROPERTY BACK).<br /> <br /> From Bruce Lee in the 70s to the huge selection of fighting video games, Sentai style shows like the Power Rangers and anime, our culture has soaked up little bits of the martial arts. Pop culture, sure, but counterculture and hobbyists tend to bend pop until it's not. Think about a thing you think of as niche. It was probably popular somewhere at some point. A friend of mine has been running an rpg game based on Dragon Ball Z for over ten years, which he designed himself all the way from the dice mechanics to the computer algorithms he could use to automatically update and adjust for all status changes in the game by simply entering the dice results. It's...crazy, and awesome. But it's also a geeky labor of love.<br /> <br /> I've met gamers in fighting gyms, dojos and rougher places. There are trained soldiers, Brazilian Jiu-jutsu practitioners and at least one boxer on these forums that I know of. That's not counting myself, <b><i>the greatest sword fighter in the world.</i></b><br /> <br /> <b>So, let's talk about Martial Arts.</b><br /> Got in a fight? Have a certain interest? What do YOU know, personally? What have you read? Have some interesting information? Perhaps you have a hypothetical situation, a question you'd like answered or something you'd like examined/to discuss in a fashion you haven't seen elsewhere?<br /> <br /> This is the place to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 10-05-2015, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T22:55:04-07:00","id":689349,"title":"","content":"Man I'd love to take a martial art...but i dont even know where to begin, or what type would suit me...I dont do complicated at all, I'm so uncooridinated its hillarious, and i cannot for the life of me follow directions even visual unless its repeated many times.<br /> <br /> On a silly semi related note does yoga count as a martial art?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T02:28:28-07:00","id":689507,"title":"","content":"I've been into martial art since I was twelve, so I've got more than fifteen years under my belt* (Mostly shotokan and shito-ryu karate.) I did a bit of krav maga and a few years of fencing (\u00e9p\u00e9e) too. All in all, I'm pretty good, but I never did a lot of competing : I love training, but I don't really like tournaments.<br /> <br /> I've been in a few street fights too, mostly because I'm something of a hot-blooded asshole at times (I'll never outright attack someone, but I will look for trouble if I get the impression that someone is being bothersome to others.) I'm getting better at resolving tense situations without punching anyone, so that's good (especially when one considers the way males in my family tend to act.) I think my martial arts training helped me be more peaceful too : it's easier not to loose control if a fight does erupt, and simply being perfectly calm in the face of potential violence is often enought to discourage people from picking a fight.<br /> <br /> I'd love to go train in a monastery for a few month if I ever get the chance, but my studies and work are currently keeping me busy enought that I don't know if I'll get to do it for at least a few years.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I tend to incorporate martial arts into my stories, both in rpgs (one of the many reasons I love Exalted) and in writing (one of the protagonist of my current webfiction is a martial artist).<br /> <br /> *and yes, pun intented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T02:40:52-07:00","id":689517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/688727-the-martial-arts-thread?p=689349#post689349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man I'd love to take a martial art...but i dont even know where to begin, or what type would suit me...I dont do complicated at all, I'm so uncooridinated its hillarious, and i cannot for the life of me follow directions even visual unless its repeated many times.<br /> <br /> On a silly semi related note does yoga count as a martial art?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to be coordinated to start, that's the point : you'll get better at it if you train ^^. As for what type would suit you, it really depends on whether you'd rather like to learn how to kick and punch people (in which case, try a hard style like karate or taekwondo), learn to control your body (soft styles like wing chun and t'ai chi ch'uan focus on perfect mastery of your movements, often by training very slowly until you master the moves enough to do them without thinking), or something else (krav maga is perfect if you want to learn self-defense, ju-jitsu is good for both self-defense and control, capoeira is extremely fun to practise and it's almost a dance despite being somewhat effective.)<br /> <br /> And no, I don't think yoga is considered to be a martial art (though if I recall correctly, some stances at least are inspired, if not directly taken from, indian martial disciplines). It can be a good basis for training though (you'll find some stances familiar, learn to keep your balance and control your body and breating... all that is useful and more.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T03:09:22-07:00","id":689525,"title":"","content":"I've done Judo, T'ai chi chuan and Capoeira. I once competed in Judo, but that was an eternity ago. I'd like to get back to it as it did me a lot of good mentally and physically. I always liked working on mastering a movement, both on in term of effectiveness and aesthetism. It bring a welcome clarity to one's mind, I've found.<br /> I'm very interested in learning Aikido, Muay Thai, Taekwondo, Vovinam Viet Vo Dao or Pencak Silat one of these days, but I'm not sure which I should choose.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T06:31:30-07:00","id":689636,"title":"","content":"So there's this Western Martial Arts competition called the &quot;Battle of the Nations&quot;. Each participant country fields a team that puts on medieval arms and armor and they beat the shit out of each other until they can't get up anymore. For most teams, the average participant is 24 and a member of their country's Special Forces. For the US Team, the youngest member is 40 and most are members of the SCA (i.e. history geeks). The only reason Team USA didn't roll the competition their first year was that they had never practiced together before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T07:12:24-07:00","id":689670,"title":"","content":"I've been taking Tai Chi for about five years now. Yang style from the 24 form, the 48, and the 108. We've also learned a staff form and a sword form. We're now actually learning Ba Gua. Our class is not a sparing class, we only do forms for health, balance, and coordination. <br /> <br /> I've really enjoyed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T20:21:41-07:00","id":690803,"title":"","content":"I like martial arts! My primary styles are capoeira Angola, Bujinkan bud\u014d taijutsu, and scholastic wrestling. I'm also familiar with Ch\u00e9n style t\u00e0ij\u00ed boxing and aikid\u014d, and I've taken a lesson or two in many other disciplines (kenp\u014d, systema, serrada, fencing, b\u0101gu\u00e0, Yagy\u016b Shinkage-ry\u016b \u2026). I am always happy to fight anyone who's nice to me.<br /> <br /> Anteros, with what group/teacher do you play?<br /> <br /> I have lots of thoughts about how to start/choose a martial art\u2014I'll see if I can dig up the essay I wrote for someone on the forums about it\u2014but the short answer is &quot;go to all the schools in your area which are convenient, then keep attending the one with the people you like the best, regardless of style.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T00:24:54-07:00","id":690942,"title":"","content":"We had a Capoeira club at the university but it's been over 5 years now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T20:17:13-07:00","id":691916,"title":"","content":"Took Taekwondo years ago(and I mean years ago). Sadly had to leave it because of parents. The week before my Red belt exam too(in my school it would have been two more then black belt). Never went back. Don't think my Master still teaches, but I believe his Master's school is still open. Don't think my old gamers body is up to trying to learn from him if he is still teaching here. Real old school master from Korea(his Master was a Grandmaster still living in Korea at the time). Back then he went to Korea for his 7th Dan(I think) the year before I quit. Took a little Judo and didn't care for it. Had a horrible Kung Fu Master for a semester. Always wanted to try Akido, but the nearest is 2 hours away and I just can't manage that on my schedule and family matters.<br /> <br /> If talking martial in the full sense, then I took fencing for a year and a half. Always meant to go back. Again lucky enough to get a great trainer. He went to the olympics a few times when he was younger. He taught fencing Foil, Epee, and Saber<br /> <br /> If I was in better shape it might all mean something. Right now don't think I could beat up a fly. I've been lucky in teachers and opportunity, but a poor student. Can blame some of it on health and some of it on time, but ultimately can only blame myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Does that mean I can to register my hands as lethal bunnies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 10-06-2015, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T08:44:56-07:00","id":692522,"title":"","content":"Been studying American Kenpo for the past few years. I'm up to purple belt (7th class) right now and had to take a long break from my studies because I was living in a place where there was no teacher to help me advance. I've moved back to a place where I can find a teacher, though, and found a school that looks promising. I'm working to get back into shape so that I can look like a purple belt when I meet the teacher.<br /> <br /> That's something I really like about the martial arts: It's not enough to have a certain rank, or even a certificate for a it. You have to move like someone who deserves that rank if you want to keep it at your new school.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:23:55-07:00","id":692589,"title":"","content":"I do boxing as an exercise. Haven't ever used it against another person. I'm a little afraid to since I make that 75 lbs heavy bag (and the metal rack it's on) swing around quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T16:00:42-07:00","id":694262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/688727-the-martial-arts-thread?p=692589#post692589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do boxing as an exercise. Haven't ever used it against another person. I'm a little afraid to since I make that 75 lbs heavy bag (and the metal rack it's on) swing around quite a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty normal, in all honesty. Boxing is an excellent exercise, but it's even more of a workout when it's done against a live opponent. You'll find that your power disappears pretty quickly against someone who's throwing punches back at you. : )<br /> <br /> I used to box. A lot. Did so for 7 years, and took it extremely seriously. I even have an amateur record of 1-1. I wish I was joking. Stopped in 1999, however, since college was kicking my ass.<br /> <br /> The only martial art I compete in now is archery. Which I'm not exactly sure is even considered a martial art. I do it because I love it and find it more challenging than shooting guns--which I also do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T00:00:02-07:00","id":696825,"title":"","content":"I started with Judo which was pretty much obligatory where I came from. Got until the Blue Belt before I quit due to an injury and fought at a few tournaments. Never got first place, but the occasional third and second which wasn't half bad considering how many people participated.<br /> <br /> The one I did the longest was Muay Thai which I did 'til Khan 7. I would have kept going on, but sadly my Trainer decided to leave and I couldn't for the life of me click with the new one. Its one thing to teach people Martial Arts at a competetive level but a whole other one to solely focus on that. I never liked the idea of fighting exclusively to win, as pretentious as this may sound, so I quit. I actually won a full-contact tournament in Muay-Thai once but that sounds far more impressive than it actually was due to the fact that I was in a weight class that only had four contestants.<br /> <br /> Currently I'm doing Monkey Kung-Fu and Ninjutsu, but not too seriously. Sadly, I don't have the time to do so. I also dabbled in Capoeira, Iado and Taekwondo, but not on any &quot;real&quot; level.<br /> <br /> Concerning fights I always try to avoid them, either by trying to de-escalate the situation or, if nothing else, running. One time I actually failed at both and had to defend myself physically which I'm still glad I managed. My Muay-Thai teacher always said that we should consider everyone we fight to be potentially stronger than us. Does he carry a knife? Or maybe even a gun? Will he call for backup or use dirty tricks? And if nothing else helps hit first and hit hard so he can't use any of those advantages. I'm still grateful to him for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T22:24:48-07:00","id":1114439,"title":"","content":"Thinking about getting back into Baguazhang and Wing Chun. Those were my old standards and styles I found intuitive for me, so it's a good reintroduction to training. I've considered giving Muay Thai and BJJ a chance, just because of the quality of sparring with the mma scene in Albuquerque, but I'll likely hold off for a good while. The Gracie BJJ school near my house is well respected, so that would probably be my first choice for new study.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T07:19:01-07:00","id":1114572,"title":"","content":"I used to train in Shorin-Ryu and Kempo, plus a little cross training in Judo and Kickboxing. Unfortunately I've been on the couch for the better part of four years now. I'd love to get back into it, but its matter of finding the teacher and tuition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T15:31:38-07:00","id":1114783,"title":"","content":"I need to get back into Kick-Boxing myself. I miss my pals there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}